---
import Layout from '~/layouts/PageLayout.astro';

const metadata = {
  title: 'Terms of Service - LifeWebLab',
};
---

<Layout metadata={metadata}>
  <section class="px-6 sm:px-6 py-12 sm:py-16 lg:py-20 mx-auto max-w-4xl">
    <header class="mb-8 md:mb-12 text-center">
      <h1
        class="text-3xl sm:text-4xl md:text-5xl font-bold leading-tighter tracking-tighter mb-4 font-heading dark:text-gray-200"
      >
        Terms of Service
      </h1>
      <p class="text-muted dark:text-slate-400 text-sm">Last updated: October 28, 2026</p>
    </header>

    <div
      class="mx-auto prose prose-lg dark:prose-invert max-w-none text-gray-700 dark:text-gray-300 leading-relaxed space-y-6"
    >
      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">1. Acceptance of Terms</h2>
      <p>
        By accessing <strong>LifeWebLab</strong> (<a href="https://lifeweblab.com" class="text-primary hover:underline"
          >https://lifeweblab.com</a
        >), you agree to comply with these terms of service, all applicable laws and regulations, and acknowledge that
        you are responsible for compliance with any applicable local laws. If you do not agree with any of these terms,
        you are prohibited from using or accessing this site.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">2. Financial & Payment Troubleshooting Disclaimer</h2>
      <p>
        The technical guides, payment gateway troubleshooting steps, billing architectures, and cross-border invoicing
        procedures published on LifeWebLab are provided strictly for educational, informational, and technical
        diagnostics purposes. LifeWebLab is an independent publication and does not operate as a financial institution,
        licensed escrow agent, or registered payment processor.
      </p>
      <p>
        Payment processing rules, banking policies, interchange fees, and regulatory requirements (such as Stripe,
        PayPal, Wise, or banking networks) change continuously. LifeWebLab shall not be held liable for direct or
        indirect losses, transaction fees, chargebacks, currency fluctuations, or account suspensions incurred through
        the implementation of published guides. Users are encouraged to verify critical transaction configurations with
        their respective financial providers or official API documentation.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">3. Intellectual Property & Technical Workflows</h2>
      <p>
        All original editorial content, diagnostic diagrams, procedural frameworks, and proprietary analyses on
        LifeWebLab are protected by applicable copyright and intellectual property laws. Readers are permitted to apply
        and implement published troubleshooting procedures in their personal or commercial billing environments.
        However, automated scraping, uncredited syndication, or mass reproduction without explicit prior written
        authorization is strictly prohibited.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">4. Revisions & Errata</h2>
      <p>
        Due to frequent API deprecations and policy changes by international financial networks, technical materials
        appearing on LifeWebLab may include updates or revisions. We reserve the right to revise, improve, or update
        technical materials and documentation at any time without prior notice.
      </p>

      <h2 class="text-2xl font-bold mt-8 mb-4">5. Governing Law</h2>
      <p>
        These terms and conditions are governed by and construed in accordance with applicable legal frameworks, and you
        irrevocably submit to the exclusive jurisdiction of the competent courts for any legal matters arising
        hereunder.
      </p>
    </div>
  </section>
</Layout>
